# Astrolabe ESP MCP

When debugging Astrolabe on hardware, **do not guess** from compile-only checks — capture and review the USB console.

## Automatic console review (default)

| Situation | Tool |
|-----------|------|
| After flash, boot check, crash repro, face swipe bug | **`astrolabe_console_review`** |
| Raw log only (no triage) | `astrolabe_serial_monitor` |
| Upload + boot triage | `astrolabe_build_upload_monitor` |

**`astrolabe_console_review`** captures serial, detects panics/reboot loops/WiFi+BT coexistence, and writes:

- `artifacts/monitor/latest.log` — full text
- `artifacts/monitor/latest-review.json` — `boot_ok`, `issues`, sample errors

Typical calls:

- Boot after flash: `duration_sec=30`, `reset_boot=true`, `stop_pattern="PocketMynah MVP ready"`
- Repro without reset: `reset_boot=false`, `duration_sec=20`
- Inject serial command: `send_line="face 3"` (QA face index)

Read `status=HEALTHY` vs `NEEDS ATTENTION` and `issues=` in the tool result before continuing.

Shell fallback: `./scripts/console_review.sh 30`

## Other tools

| Need | MCP tool |
|------|----------|
| Serial + JTAG adapter smoke test | `astrolabe_console_monitor` |
| OpenOCD link only | `astrolabe_jtag_openocd` |
| Halt / backtrace / inject face | `astrolabe_jtag_gdb` / `astrolabe_debug_gdb` |
| List `/dev/cu.usbmodem*` | `astrolabe_list_ports` |
| Flash | `astrolabe_upload` / `astrolabe_build` |

JTAG does **not** stream `printf` — pair GDB with **`astrolabe_console_review`**.

## Clock-face QA

Follow [hardware-qa.mdc](hardware-qa.mdc): upload → `astrolabe_console_review` (boot ok) → show face → `screen.bmp`.

Reload MCP after changing `mcp/astrolabe-esp/` (`./mcp/astrolabe-esp/setup.sh`, entry in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`).
